#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:2
msgid "An Intro to the GUI"
msgstr "GUI 介紹"

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:7
msgid "Folder View"
msgstr "資料夾檢視"

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:9
msgid ""
"The left side of the screen shows the ID and current state of all configured "
"folders. Clicking the folder name makes that section expand to show more "
"detailed folder information, and buttons for pausing the folder, forcing a "
"rescan, or editing the configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:14
msgid "A folder can be in any one of these states:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:16
msgid "Unknown"
msgstr "未知"

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:17
msgid "while the GUI is loading,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:19
msgid "Unshared"
msgstr "未共享"

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:20
msgid "when you have not shared this folder yet,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:22
msgid "Paused"
msgstr "已暫停"

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:23
msgid "when the folder's activity has been put on hold,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:25
msgid "Stopped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:26
msgid "when the folder has experienced an error,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:28
msgid "Up to Date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:29
msgid "when the folder is in sync with the rest of the devices,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:31
msgid "Waiting to Scan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:32
msgid "when waiting for other folders to idle before scanning the folder,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:34
msgid "Scanning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:35
msgid "while Syncthing is looking in the folder for local changes,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:37
msgid "Waiting to Sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:38
msgid "when waiting for other folders to idle before syncing the folder,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:40
msgid "Preparing to Sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:41
msgid "when Syncthing is gathering file changes to synchronize,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:43
msgid "Syncing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:44
msgid "when this device is downloading changes from the network,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:46
msgid "Waiting to Clean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:47
msgid "when waiting for the folder to idle before cleaning versions,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:49
msgid "Cleaning Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:50
msgid "while removing obsolete files from the .stversions folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:52
msgid "Local Additions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:53
msgid ""
"when locally added or modified items are present in a receive-only folder, "
"thus not synced to remote machines.  The red button \"Revert Local Changes\" "
"will revert and delete all local changes to the state advertised by remote "
"devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:58
msgid ""
"Among the folder details, you can see the current \"Global State\" and "
"\"Local State\" summaries, as well as the amount of \"Out of Sync\" data if "
"the folder state is not up to date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:62
msgid "Global State"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:63
msgid ""
"indicates how much data the fully up to date folder contains, which is "
"basically the sum of the newest versions of all files from all connected "
"devices. This is the size of the folder on your computer when it is fully in "
"sync with the remote devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:68
msgid "Local State"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:69
msgid ""
"shows how much data the folder actually contains right now. This can be more "
"or less than the global state, if the folder is currently synchronizing with "
"other devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:73
msgid "Out of Sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:74
msgid ""
"shows how much data needs to be synchronized from other devices. Note that "
"this is the sum of all out of sync *files* - if you already have parts of "
"such a file, or an older version of the file, less data than this will need "
"to be transferred over the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:79
msgid "Error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:80
msgid ""
"describes the problem when the folder is in state Stopped. One possible "
"message is \"folder marker missing\". This means that the root directory of "
"this folder does not contain a file or directory called ``.stfolder`` "
"(marker). Syncthing stops when this marker goes missing to prevent data loss "
"e.g. when the folder path was unmounted. If the marker was deleted "
"accidentally, just recreate it and press the rescan button in the UI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:89
msgid "Creating a new synced folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:91
msgid ""
"Use the Syncthing Web interface. Click the \"Add Folder\" button which will "
"bring up a dialogue with the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:94
msgid "Folder Label"
msgstr "資料夾標籤"

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:95
msgid ""
"should be set to something descriptive. This label will initially be shared "
"with remote devices, but can be changed on each device, as desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:99
msgid "Folder ID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:100
msgid ""
"has to be the same across all devices, as it is the unique identifier of the "
"folder. Best practice is to keep the auto-generated ID to avoid conflicts "
"with equally named folders on other devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:104
msgid "Folder Path"
msgstr "資料夾路徑"

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:105
msgid "designates the physical path to the folder, i.e. on your hard drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:107
msgid ""
"Next select with which devices to share the folder with and press add, which "
"will add the folder and start syncing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:111
msgid "Device View"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../intro/gui.rst:113
msgid ""
"The right side of the screen shows the overall state of all configured "
"devices. The local device is always at the top, with remote devices in "
"alphabetical order below. For each device you see its current state and, "
"when expanded, more detailed information. All transfer rates (\"Download "
"Rate\" and \"Upload Rate\") are from the perspective of the local device, "
"even those shown for remote devices. The rates for the local device are the "
"sum of those for the remote devices. For each rate, you can see the current "
"transfer speed, followed by the total amount of data transferred so far. You "
"can click the current transfer speed to toggle the units between bytes and "
"bits."
msgstr ""
